      "writtenOn": "2021-06-07T15:07:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why place this requirement? It would be easier to use this class if it took care of adopting the shell permission identity whenever it needed it.\n\nI think adoptShellPermissionIdentity calls don\u0027t nest, so you can\u0027t just adopt/drop shell permission identity in this class, because if the caller had already adopted the permission identity, then this class would drop it.\n\nBut perhaps you could call checkPermission to see if the code has the MANAGE_TEST_NETWORKS_PERMISSION, and if it doesn\u0027t, then adopt the shell permission identity and note that fact? Might be as simple as:\n\n    private void runWithManageTestNetworksPermission(ThrowingRunnable r) {\n        if (sContext.checkSelfPermission(MANAGE_TEST_NETWORKS)) {\n            r.run();\n        } else {\n            runWithShellPermissionIdentity(r, MANAGE_TEST_NETWORKS);\n        }\n    }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 59,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 53
      },
